- -O2 tail calls: return f(args) -> jmp f. Still open for multiple arguments
  (needs the same argument-overlap care GCC's sibcall pass takes --
  see torture/20050713-1.c's own comment).

- -O2 performance: IR backend for eligible functions

  Problem. -O2 is currently as slow as -O0 (bench: 763 vs 786 ms; AWFY 6499 vs
  6504 ms), slower than TCC, ~4x behind gcc -O2 and antcc. Kernel timings (ms):
      kernel   rcc -O2   antcc   gcc -O0   gcc -O2
      sum        1217      929     3417       671
      axpy       2262      606     3615       234
      fib         431      323      393        82
      norm       5219     1209     2743       649
      mm         2062      376     1049       260
  On norm and mm rcc -O2 is slower than gcc -O0.

  Causes (all in the AST-walking codegen, not in opt.c):
  - hot-local promotion (codegen.c "-O2+: hot scalar locals") is 3 regs
    (rbx, r12, r13), int/long/ptr only, params excluded: no FP, no structs,
    loop bounds reloaded from the stack each iteration.
  - float/double values live in GPR vregs: every op is movq xmm<->gpr + mulsd.
  - no scaled-index addressing for a[i]/p->f (shl+movslq+add per access);
    no memory-operand ALU/FP forms in the asm layer.
  - loops test at the top plus a back jmp; ?: and if materialize setcc+movzx+cmp.
  - oversized frames for leaf functions, scalar returns round-trip the stack,
    "mov $0,%eax" before non-variadic calls.
  - the -O3 ssa_rename_pass renames then un-renames: no pass consumes SSA, so
    -O3 == -O2. CSE is a tiny ring buffer; ssa_unroll is disabled.
  - inliner only takes single-return-expression callees.

  Plan: Do not add more special cases to the
  tree codegen; lower eligible functions to a basic-block SSA IR instead:
    AST -> IR -> mem2reg (Braun et al., no dominance frontiers) -> IR passes
        -> linear-scan regalloc (loop-weighted spill cost, ABI fixed intervals,
           copy hints) -> isel with address folding -> existing x86_* encoder.
  - Per-function eligibility, fallback to the current codegen otherwise: scalar
    int/ptr/float/double, loads/stores, calls, structured control flow. Not
    eligible: VLA, asm, complex, int128/bitint/decimal/vector, setjmp, cleanup,
    nested fns, computed goto.
  - x86-64 first; ARM64 keeps the old path until an IR emitter exists.
  - Retire the dead AST CFG/dom/DF/phi code and the no-op -O3 rename pass once
    the IR consumes SSA.

  Steps:
  0. DONE: IR and old-codegen functions share one object (no CFI to keep
     in sync; -g/ubsan/asan/stack-protector TUs disable the IR path).
  1. DONE: ir_build (Braun SSA), ir_opt (fold/DCE/GVN/LICM), ir_x86
     (address folding, linear-scan regalloc, emit). Calls (direct/indirect,
     variadic, stack args), struct field access, globals (plain + GOT),
     ZERO_INIT, GNU `?:`. ~70% of unit-test functions go through the IR.
     Kernels (ms, was -> now; antcc): sum 1217->938 (929), axpy 2262->520
     (606), norm 5219->662 (1209), mm 2062->288 (376), fib 431->349 (323).
     Suites green at -O2 and default: 431/431 units, TCC 118/118, torture 0.
  2. DONE (builder): struct/union copies and array assignment (unrolled
     copies / memcpy), calls with aggregate args (VALUE8/VALUE16/PTR/MEMORY per
     ir_agg_class, mirroring the AST codegen's SysV simplification), aggregate
     params (incl. >16B MEMORY-class copies to local storage), struct returns
     (two-reg RAX:RDX for all-integer <=16B, hidden __retbuf pointer otherwise),
     switch (compare chains incl. case ranges, Duff's device, fallthrough),
     goto/labels, GNU statement expressions, casts on address spines.
     IR ABI encoding: arg_class/param_class entries (bytes<<3)|class;
     CALL.ret_agg >0 = two-reg return, <0 = sret. Backend aggregate support in
     ir_x86.c. Wider eligibility: ~77% of unit-test functions.
     Remaining rejections: bitfields, inline asm, atomics, volatile, complex/
     decimal/int128/long double, labeled loops (C2Y), special callees.
  3. PARTLY DONE: IR inliner (small same-TU callees without frame slots,
     multi-block/multi-return bodies spliced before ir_opt; IR built for the
     whole TU up front so callees defined later inline too; respects the new
     __attribute__((noinline)) flag, which the AST inliner now honors as well;
     call-heavy benchmark 0.21s -> 0.13s, gcc -O2 0.14s). Redundant-load
     elimination, store-to-load forwarding (exact-width and exact TRUNC/SEXT/
     ZEXT cases), dead-store elimination and non-escaping frame-slot analysis
     in ir_opt. Still open: inline callees with frame slots (rebase slots),
     recursive-call tail calls to loops, loads/stores across join points
     (needs dataflow instead of the dominator-tree walk), LICM of loads with
     alias info, induction-variable widening and strength reduction, loop
     rotation, memory operands in ALU/FP ops, scalar replacement of
     non-escaping structs and arrays (AWFY).
  4. ARM64 IR emitter.

  Gate every step on `./run_tests "./rcc -O2" --all --parallel`

- interchange and extended float types (just aliased, no __STDC_IEC_60559_TYPES__)
